=== layout: stacked-panels

# Three Tetrad Classes

@top

![two gene classes](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/two_gene_classes.svg)

@bottom

- *PD*: only parental combinations, ab and ++.
- *NPD*: only nonparental combinations, a+ and +b.
- *TT*: all four combinations, one of each.

=== layout: two-panels

# Add the Tetrads in Each Class

@left

![Two-gene tetrad working table](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/two_gene_table_classified.svg)

@right

[*Step 3: Test Linkage*]{color=#6C6C00}

Add the counts of all PD, NPD, and TT sets.

Are PD and NPD approximately equal?

- Given parents: ++ / ab.
- Total: 1,000 tetrads.

