Spores shown for A-B. Count tetrads, not individual spores.

=== layout: two-panels

# A and B Are Linked

@left

![Two-gene tetrad working table](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/two_gene_table_classified.svg)

@right

[*Step 3: Test Linkage*]{color=#6C6C00}

- PD = 650.
- NPD = 10.
- TT = 340.
- PD is much greater than NPD: *linked*.
- Check: 650 + 10 + 340 = 1,000.

- Given parents: ++ / ab.
- Total: 1,000 tetrads.

@citation

Spores shown for A-B. Count tetrads, not individual spores.

=== layout: one-panel

# Use the Linked-Gene Formula

@body

- TT, NPD, and N are tetrad counts.
- N includes all tetrads, including PD.

$$
D = \frac{\frac{1}{2}TT + 3NPD}{N} \times 100 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

- We already tested linkage. Now substitute the counts.

=== layout: two-panels

# Substitute the Two-Gene Counts

@left

![Two-gene tetrad working table](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/two_gene_table_classified.svg)

@right

[*Step 4: Calculate Distance*]{color=#007A00}

$$
D = \frac{\frac{1}{2}(340) + 3(10)}{1000} \times 100 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

Calculate the numerator first.

- Given parents: ++ / ab.
- Total: 1,000 tetrads.

@citation

Spores shown for A-B. Count tetrads, not individual spores.

=== layout: two-panels

# A to B: 20 cM

@left

![Two-gene tetrad working table](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/two_gene_table_classified.svg)

@right

[*Step 4: Calculate Distance*]{color=#007A00}

$$
D = \frac{170 + 30}{1000} \times 100 = 20 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

The weighted count is 200; the total is 1,000 tetrads.

- Given parents: ++ / ab.
- Total: 1,000 tetrads.

@citation

Spores shown for A-B. Count tetrads, not individual spores.

=== layout: one-panel

# Recombination Is Not Map Distance

@body

- Observed recombination counts recombinant spores.
- The corrected map estimate accounts for additional crossovers.
- The same tetrads give two answers because we are measuring different things.

$$
RF = \frac{\frac{1}{2}(340) + 10}{1000} \times 100 = 18\%
$$

$$
D = \frac{\frac{1}{2}(340) + 3(10)}{1000} \times 100 = 20 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

@notes

Ask what changed between the formulas: the NPD weight changes from one to three. The correction adds 2 cM here. We still observed 18% recombinant spores; estimating hidden exchanges does not change those observed genotypes.

